From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 14:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/cix: edp-panel: read desc properties via
 device_property, default bpc/bus_format on ACPI

cix_edp_panel_of_get_desc_data() is only ever reached when the ACPI
match table's driver_data is unset (platform_acpi_match[] has
{ .id = "CIXH5040", .driver_data = 0 } -- no static panel_desc), so
on this ACPI-boot platform (confirmed live, Orion O6N 2026-07-18)
it is the only path that ever runs. But the whole function reads via
of_-only APIs (dev->of_node is NULL on ACPI): of_child_node_is_present
always fails, so num_modes/num_timings stay 0, and the bpc/bus-format/
width-mm/height-mm reads never even execute (gated behind
`if (desc->num_modes || desc->num_timings)`).

Confirmed via ACPI DSDT disassembly that CIXH5040 _DSD DOES provide
width-mm (0x81) and height-mm (0xAB) -- real panel dimensions -- but
the driver silently never picks them up because of_property_read_u32()
cannot read from a non-existent OF node. bpc and bus-format are
genuinely absent from this platform _DSD (a firmware/BIOS gap, not
fixable in-kernel), so default them to the standard 8bpc /
MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RGB888_1X24 -- the near-universal default for 24-bit
eDP when unspecified -- rather than leaving them at 0/invalid and
warning on every boot.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/cix_edp_panel.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/cix_edp_panel.c
index 114127c..5dbe57f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/cix_edp_panel.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/cix_edp_panel.c
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@
 #include <drm/drm_panel.h>
 #include <linux/acpi.h>
 #include <linux/backlight.h>
+#include <linux/media-bus-format.h>
 #include "cix_edp_panel.h"
 
 /**
@@ -799,12 +800,20 @@ static int cix_edp_panel_of_get_desc_data(struct device *dev,
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (desc->num_modes || desc->num_timings) {
-		of_property_read_u32(np, "bpc", &desc->bpc);
-		of_property_read_u32(np, "bus-format", &desc->bus_format);
-		of_property_read_u32(np, "width-mm", &desc->size.width);
-		of_property_read_u32(np, "height-mm", &desc->size.height);
-	}
+	/*
+	 * device_property_* works on both OF and ACPI (_DSD); the platform's
+	 * ACPI CIXH5040 device provides width-mm/height-mm but no bpc or
+	 * bus-format, so fall back to the standard 8bpc/RGB888 default
+	 * rather than leaving these at 0 (invalid).
+	 */
+	device_property_read_u32(dev, "bpc", &desc->bpc);
+	device_property_read_u32(dev, "bus-format", &desc->bus_format);
+	device_property_read_u32(dev, "width-mm", &desc->size.width);
+	device_property_read_u32(dev, "height-mm", &desc->size.height);
+	if (desc->bus_format == 0)
+		desc->bus_format = MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RGB888_1X24;
+	if (desc->bpc != 6 && desc->bpc != 8)
+		desc->bpc = 8;
 
 	device_property_read_u32(dev, "prepare-delay-ms", &desc->delay.prepare);
 	device_property_read_u32(dev, "enable-delay-ms", &desc->delay.enable);
